# Bottom Navigation Layout Rules

Locked files: `src/components/BottomNav.tsx`, `src/components/bottom-nav.module.css`, `src/hooks/usePinBottomNav.ts`, rendered once as a **direct child of `<body>`** in `src/app/layout.tsx`. Do not add a second nav in pages.

- Do NOT `position: fixed` on `html`. Do NOT make `body` a flex column or `overflow-y: auto`.
- Do NOT put `env(safe-area-inset-bottom)` on the tab bar as height, padding, or margin. iOS Home Screen already parks `position:fixed; bottom:0` on the safe edge; adding env lifts the icons and leaves an empty band above the home indicator.
- CSS fallback: `bottom: 0`, `height: 52px`, `padding: 0`, `transform: none`. JS (`usePinBottomNav`) pins the 52px icon row to the lowest paintable pixel (`visualViewport` / `bottom:0` probe). Do not add Tailwind `pb-*` / `mb-*` / `pb-safe` on the nav.
- Do NOT hide the nav on route change.

Every route uses `PageShell` with `w-full min-h-full pb-[70px] pt-[env(safe-area-inset-top)] bg-background`.
`PageHeader` is not sticky.
